<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amalia pours first North West project gold.</title>
<headline>Amalia pours first North West project gold.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amalia Gold Mining and Exploration Co Ltd said on Monday it poured its first gold on September 12 from its North West Province goldfield project near the Botswanan border.</p>
<p>The company said gold pouring capacity would escalate sharply, rising to 30 kg a month by the year-end, to 45 kg by mid-1997 and to 70 kg a month in 18 months time.  </p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
